# Sensitive paths for shipping-work-python-fastapi's doc-check.sh (Step 1.5).
# One path per line; blank lines and #-comments ignored. Entries match whole
# path SEGMENTS at any depth. This file REPLACES the script's built-in
# defaults wholesale — it does not extend them (#75, gregoryfoster/skills#252).
#
# Guarded by tests/test_doc_sensitive_paths.py: a dead entry is a red test
# here, not a note under a green gate run.
#
# Five defaults are dropped because this tree cannot match them. Replicator has
# no DB (schema.sql, alembic/versions/, src/models/), no changelog
# (CHANGELOG.md), and ships no committed env template (.env.example) — config
# lives in /etc/replicator/.env, see docs/ENVIRONMENT.md.

# Agent- and human-facing entry points. AGENTS.md inventories the rest.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
README.md

# Dependency surface: the co-core pin and the wheelhouse story are documented
# prose, not just lockfile state (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md).
pyproject.toml
uv.lock

# Module layout. Whole tree, not the per-package list the defaults used: a NEW
# top-level package under src/ is exactly the change that leaves AGENTS.md's
# Project Layout stale, and a per-package list would miss it.
src/

# Runnable surface — docs/COMMANDS.md lists every script with its flags.
scripts/

# The systemd unit and its guards (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md, Server Lifecycle).
deploy/

# CI gates, including the charter enforcement in tests/test_boundaries.py.
.github/workflows/

# Normative contracts — linked from sibling repos, so drift here is cross-repo.
#
# The rest of docs/ is deliberately absent, and that is a trade-off rather than
# an oversight: AGENTS.md's Detail Docs list is a by-name inventory of
# docs/*.md, so adding docs/FOO.md does need an AGENTS.md line and this gate
# will not ask for it. A blanket docs/ entry would instead fire on every branch
# that edits documentation prose — which is most of them — and a gate that
# always fires is one nobody reads. Structural drift under docs/ is accepted as
# uncaught to keep the gate's exit 1 meaningful.
docs/contracts/

# Skill inventory, mirrored in two places and inventoried by docs/SKILLS.md.
#
# skills-vendor/ is deliberately absent: the daily auto-refresh bumps those
# pointers with no doc consequence, so listing them would trip the gate on
# every refresh commit. .gitmodules is the low-churn stand-in — it changes only
# when the vendor inventory itself changes, which is when the table in
# docs/SKILLS.md goes stale.
#
# .claude/settings.json earns its own entry: docs/SKILLS.md records hook
# suspension as an edit *there* with the hook script left in place, so a hook
# can be enabled, disabled or repointed with nothing under .claude/hooks/
# changing at all.
#
# .claude/skills/ is redundant for matching — segment matching already makes
# skills/ hit */skills/* — and is kept deliberately, for the dead-entry census
# rather than the match: it is what reports that tree emptying.
skills/
.claude/skills/
.claude/hooks/
.claude/settings.json
.gitmodules

# The list must cover itself. Editing it is precisely the change that obsoletes
# its own section in docs/SKILLS.md, and a doc-drift guard blind to its own
# configuration is the one blind spot it can least afford. Slash-less, so it
# matches at any depth and adds no churn.
doc-sensitive-paths

# The SocratiCode manifest is a source, not the artifact — editing it without
# re-indexing leaves the highest-authority answer stale (docs/SOCRATICODE.md).
.socraticodecontextartifacts.json
